     "category": "counter",
     "unit": "count",
     "scale": "raw",
     "confidence": 0.6,
     "rationale": "A single byte that always increases within a pass and wraps 3 times per pass, 1-255 range, median step of 3 between received frames. This is a rolling sequence number, so its 34 resets are wraps by design, not reboots. The 0.067/s rate would be about one count per 15 s. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
