     "offset": 14,
     "name": "uptime_or_message_counter",
     "category": "counter",
     "unit": "count",
     "scale": "raw",
     "confidence": 0.417,
     "rationale": "A 3-byte little-endian counter that increases in 99% of frames with median step 1 within a pass, and has 12 resets over 532 days, the last 0.5 days before the end. That fits an uptime or telemetry-record counter that restarts on reboot. The units could be seconds or frames, and the mean rate is not reliable because of the resets and sparse sampling. [3/3 samples agree]"
    }
   ],
   "health": "Not enough evidence for battery or thermal state, since no power or temperature fields were found. The counter at offset 14 reset 12 times in 532 days, with the last reset about 0.5 days before the end of the window. If it is an uptime counter, that suggests occasional reboots, but this is uncertain because it could also be a counter that wraps or is reset by design."
